295 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 233 0 R
/E (Digital gaming libraries accumulate vast amounts of personal data, yet these records often remain unexamined at a personal level. Without a structured analytical approach, it is difficult to identify core engagement drivers or understand how session frequency impacts total time investment in a highly skewed data environment. This study addresses this gap by applying a quantitative statistical framework to model personal gaming behavior and demonstrate that digital consumption follows predictable, evidence-based patterns.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
